   "id": "RO7PD5BBQH6VB",
   "stars": 5,
   "title": "Brilliant and unique name elimination puzzle book",
   "body": "Really enjoyed this puzzle book from The Lottery Killer author. It had a twist on the name elimination theme and has a killer, a victim and a weapon to find in different ways throughout the book. It meant going though the whole book for certain names more than once and I like that it uses the whole of the book, rather than a certain chunk. Depending on the order you work the clues, you can help yourself for later with the other two parts of the puzzle by marking every object and name as you go through. The solution is not in the book, it's a QR code to the website which is great so you don't see it by accident! Great for solution, hints, more clue help. I recommend this book for anyone who enjoys name elimination type puzzles and will purchase more from them in the future.",
   "date": "Reviewed in the United Kingdom on 19 September 2026",
